Example 7 - Gaussian Elimination in Equation Form
Concept: Use equation operations to create row-echelon form, then back-substitute.
Solve the system.
x - 2y + 3z = 9-x + 3y = -4
2x - 5y + 5z = 17
Step 1: Eliminate x from Equation 2
Equation 2 + Equation 1:
(-x + 3y) + (x - 2y + 3z) = -4 + 9
y + 3z = 5
Step 2: Eliminate x from Equation 3
Equation 3 + (-2)(Equation 1):-2(x - 2y + 3z) = -2(9)-2x + 4y - 6z = -18
Now add to Equation 3:
(2x - 5y + 5z) + (-2x + 4y - 6z) = 17 - 18-y - z = -1
Step 3: Eliminate y from the new Equation 3
New Equation 3 + New Equation 2:
(-y - z) + (y + 3z) = -1 + 5
2z = 4
z = 2
Step 4: Back-substitute
z = 2
y + 3z = 5
