Example 16 - Homogeneous System
Chapter 1 Worked Examples - Page 18
Concept: A homogeneous system has all constant terms equal to zero. It always has the trivial solution.
Solve the homogeneous system.
x1 - x2 + 3x3 = 0
2x1 + x2 + 3x3 = 0
Step 1: Write the augmented matrix
[ 1  -1   3 | 0 ]
[ 2   1   3 | 0 ]
Step 2: Eliminate x1 from Row 2
R2 + (-2)R1 -> R2-2R1 = [-2, 2, -6, 0]
[2, 1, 3, 0] + [-2, 2, -6, 0]
= [0, 3, -3, 0]
[ 1  -1   3 | 0 ]
[ 0   3  -3 | 0 ]
Step 3: Scale Row 2
(1/3)R2 -> R2
[0, 3, -3, 0] becomes [0, 1, -1, 0]
[ 1  -1   3 | 0 ]
[ 0   1  -1 | 0 ]
Step 4: Clear the -1 above the leading 1
R1 + R2 -> R1
[1, -1, 3, 0] + [0, 1, -1, 0]
= [1, 0, 2, 0]
[ 1   0   2 | 0 ]
[ 0   1  -1 | 0 ]
Step 5: Use a parameter
x1 + 2x3 = 0
x2 - x3 = 0
Let x3 = t.
x1 + 2t = 0
x1 = -2t
x2 - t = 0
x2 = t
Final answer:
x1 = -2t
x2 = t
x3 = t
t is any real number.
When t = 0, the solution is (0, 0, 0), the trivial solution.
When t = 1, the solution is (-2, 1, 1), a nontrivial solution.
